.\" Man page for agent-terminal
.TH AGENT-TERMINAL 1 "November 2026" "agent-terminal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-terminal \- shared SSH terminal for a person and a coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-terminal
.I destination
[
.B --
.I ssh-options...
]
.br
.B agent-terminal
.I command
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-terminal
starts a visible SSH terminal UI in the foreground. A person types into the
terminal directly. A coding agent connected through the MCP server can inspect
recent terminal output and send input into the same SSH session. Agent input
and remote output are visible in the UI.
.PP
The application uses the local
.BR ssh (1)
client and its normal SSH configuration, identities, and host key checks. It
does not store SSH credentials. Start the visible UI before using the local
control commands or MCP tools. The UI and MCP server must run as the same local
user on the same machine.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI read " [--lines N]"
Print recent output from the active shared session. The default is 120 lines.
.TP
.BI send " TEXT"
Type
.I TEXT
into the remote SSH session and press Enter. This executes remotely and is
visible in the UI.
.TP
.B status
Check whether the shared SSH UI is running.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the MCP stdio server. This is normally launched by Codex after MCP
registration; it does not open an SSH session itself.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show CLI help. Subcommands have their own help, for example
.BR "agent-terminal read --help" .
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed version.
.TP
.B --
When starting a session, pass all following arguments directly to
.BR ssh (1).
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Send an interrupt to the remote process.
.TP
.B Page Up / Page Down
Scroll the displayed terminal.
.TP
.B F12
Exit the UI and close its SSH process.
.SH MCP TOOLS
The MCP server exposes three tools:
.TP
.B session_status
Check that the user's visible terminal session is running.
.TP
.B terminal_read
Read recent output, up to 120 lines, from the active session.
.TP
.B terminal_send
Type supplied text into the active remote SSH session and press Enter. This
runs a remote command; the user can see the input and its output in the UI.
.PP
The agent and user share the SSH session. Keep the TUI open while using these
tools. The MCP server cannot start or reconnect a session and does not provide
a chat interface.
.SH INSTALLATION
From the source directory, build and install with Cargo:
.PP
.nf
cargo install --path .
.fi
.PP
Register the MCP server with Codex:
.PP
.nf
codex mcp add agent-terminal -- "$HOME/.cargo/bin/agent-terminal" mcp
.fi
.PP
Restart Codex after registering. Install this man page in a user man directory
with:
.PP
.nf
install -Dm644 man/agent-terminal.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/agent-terminal.1
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
Start an SSH session:
.PP
.nf
agent-terminal root@server
.fi
.PP
Pass SSH options:
.PP
.nf
agent-terminal root@server -- -p 2222 -i ~/.ssh/work_key
.fi
.PP
Inspect or interact with an active session:
.PP
.nf
agent-terminal status
agent-terminal read --lines 40
agent-terminal send 'uptime'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1)
.br
Codex MCP guide: https://developers.openai.com/codex/mcp/
.SH LIMITATIONS
This is a local, single-user bridge for one TUI session. It does not manage
multiple sessions or retain a durable transcript after the UI exits.
